            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0040" n="30" xml:id="pg30"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/2066: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-11T18:00:00-04:00">March 11, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Your 194, March 6, 3 p.m., and 195, March 7, 9 a.m. The Department has found
                    your reference telegrams most helpful and particularly appreciates receiving the
                    interpretative comment and constructive suggestions contained therein. The
                    Department is bringing your suggestions to the attention of the governmental
                    organs concerned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
